# Speak with Coleman, Agamand Heirlooms and Heirloom Weapon (1820, 1821,
# 1822): the weapon after Ulag the Cleaver (1819), the Undead Defensive
# Stance quest in Brill.
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json and objects.json for the chain, Ulag and the
# four Agamand Weapon Racks; Forever's Warrior class quest list
# (data/local/quest-audit/) for the rewards: Ulag the
# Cleaver teaches Defensive Stance, Heirloom Weapon lets you choose the
# Heirloom Axe, Hammer, Dagger or Sword.
# horde/undead/01-tirisfal-glades does Ulag the Cleaver on the route; this
# guide repeats it for anyone off the route. Orc, Troll and Tauren Warriors
# take Path of Defense (1498) instead, which the game does not offer together
# with Ulag, and get their weapon from Forged Steel (1503) on the route.

step Ulag the Cleaver
  tip Deathguard Dillinger stands in Brill. Ulag waits in the mausoleum on the hill just north of town: open the gate and fight him.
  accept 1819                                 -- Deathguard Dillinger
  kill 6390 quest 1819.1
  turnin 1819                                 -- Deathguard Dillinger: Defensive Stance
  accept 1820

step Coleman Farthing
  tip Coleman Farthing is in the inn, the Gallows' End Tavern, in Brill.
  turnin 1820                                 -- Coleman Farthing
  accept 1821

step Agamand Mills
  tip The four Agamand Weapon Racks stand among the buildings of Agamand Mills, north of Brill. The mills' undead attack on sight.
  collect 7567 quest 1821.1                   -- Agamand Family Axe
  collect 7568 quest 1821.2                   -- Agamand Family Dagger
  collect 7569 quest 1821.3                   -- Agamand Family Mace
  collect 7566 quest 1821.4                   -- Agamand Family Sword

step Back to Coleman Farthing
  turnin 1821                                 -- Coleman Farthing
  accept 1822
  turnin 1822 choose 7115 7117 7116 7118      -- Coleman Farthing
